# src/apps/daemon/internal/runtime/mobilecore

## Purpose
Deep mobile runtime owner: CoreController, TUN lifecycle, canonical mobile/evasion config translation, callbacks, status, and stats. Mobilebind remains only an adapter.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `runtime` (rank 4; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (5): `config.go`, `config_test.go`, `controller.go`, `controller_test.go`, `types.go`

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `mobilecore`.
- Notable exported surface: `CheckVersionX`, `ConfigFromEvasion`, `ConfigToEvasion`, `CoreCallbackHandler`, `CoreController`, `DefaultConfig`, `InitCoreEnv`, `IsRunning`, `MobileConfig`, `NewCoreController` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/trafficstats`, `internal/platform/mobilehost`, `internal/runtime/proxy`.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/mobilebind`.

## Invariants
- Mobile runtime lifecycle and TUN ownership live here; mobilebind is translation only.
- Canonical evasion configuration is translated without creating a second default/state authority.
- `runtime` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
